#	Provisioning network for new guests (vmd(8) switch "install").
#
#	This is the interface the installing guests live on: dhcpd(8) hands them a
#	lease with the boot file "auto_install" (see the install subnet in
#	/etc/dhcpd.conf) and httpd(8) serves the sets and install.conf from
#	10.10.99.1.  It has no physical member: only taps appear on it.
#
#	Once every guest is built you can shut the network down without touching
#	the VMs:
#	    rcctl stop dhcpd?          no — that would break USERS/GUEST
#	    ifconfig veb2 down         (and remove the pf provisioning rules)
#	Keeping it in place costs nothing and makes a rebuild one command.
description "install 10.10.99.0/24 (provisioning only)"
inet 10.10.99.1 255.255.255.0 10.10.99.255
up
